A NOTE ON THIS FILE, while the Initiative is being formed.

The Code Assurance Initiative is not yet an incorporated body. It is the organisation
this standard is published under, and the steering group that will govern it is being
assembled — see docs/GOVERNANCE.md, which states plainly what is and is not true today.

Until incorporation, "The Code Assurance Initiative" in this file names the project
rather than a legal person, and the copyright in contributions remains with the parties
who made them, licensed to everyone under Apache-2.0 on the terms in LICENSE. That is
the ordinary arrangement for a young standard, and it is written down here rather than
left to be inferred, because a reader deciding whether to depend on CAI is entitled to
know exactly whose work they are relying on and under what terms.

If the Initiative incorporates, or if a contributor agreement is adopted, this file
changes and the change is recorded in CHANGELOG.md.
